thank you  [Music]  [Music]  thank you for your patience and Welcome  to our press conference I know you're  waiting for the publication of the  conclusions which are coming shortly  I've been told first may I invite the  president of the council  news foreign  foreign  foreign  determinate  yes thank you so much indeed we had a  very good European Council we do now  have a very good and solid roadmap to  keep on working on the topic of energy  prices  the leaders have given the Strategic  guidance we wanted on the proposal that  we have put on the table on Tuesday and  that will be discussed next week Tuesday  in by the energy ministers let me focus  on a few topics that we have discussed  intensively the first one is the topic  of the joint purchasing of cars here  leaders supported very much the idea to  allow companies for the joint purchase  to build consortia  and to work together and to join forces  so to increase our Common Market power  for the demand of gas there's one  binding element in it that is when we at  the beginning aggregate the demand 15  percent are binding to be aggregated as  Demand on the market together as a joint  aggregated demand  the second topic was the focus on how to  limit episodes of excessive gas prices  and this is the discussion Around The  Benchmark for gas prices the so-called  ttf  we know that the ttf reflects mainly  pipeline gas but as we see that the  market is Shifting and more and more LNG  gas is coming to the market the ttf does  not reflect the true market situation  anymore therefore we will develop a  complementary new index to reflect  better the LNG price situation and for  the meantime  we are going to establish a market  correction mechanism exactly to limit  episodes of excessive gas prices and to  make sure that there is a clear order in  uh the build of the market  so here we will work with the energy  ministers to submit a legal proposal to  operationalize this Market correction  mechanism  of course leaders also discussed a  second topic which is a potential  mechanism to limit the influence of high  gas prices on the cost of electricity  we had a Frank discussion which further  clarified on one hand the opportunities  and on the other hand highlighted the  challenges  we will analyze the financial impact of  those countries with a lot of gas in  their electricity production what does  it mean if we cap the gas to reduce the  inference of gas on the electricity  price  and the second topic which has to be  analyzed is the flow of of subsidized  electricities to non-eu neighbors here  too we will work with the member states  and with the council formation to find a  well-balanced and common approach on  these issues  the commission will also come back to  the issue of state aid next week the  college will adopt the proposal on the  prolongation and the adaptation of the  temporary crisis framework  this will give member states an improved  ability to support their companies in  the face of the current crisis while  preserving a Level Playing Field so  common rules for everybody  for example thanks to the extension of  time limits for State support or new  options to support companies reducing  the electricity mud this new revised  state aid crisis framework will be then  decided on next week in the college  moving forward to the topic of funding I  just mentioned the state at  opportunities but there's also a strong  look at the opportunity at the  possibilities to support vulnerable  households and vulnerable businesses we  are aiming to make available up to  around 40 billion euros of funds that  are still still available from the  previous mff  so with that member states will be able  to help the most affected by the energy  crisis by be it the vulnerable  households or smes but indeed more is  needed to support small and medium  companies but also larger industry to  deal with the high energy prices and  here the topic of investment is very  important the investment can be financed  through the European level that is the  vehicle re-power EU that is right now in  the process of being decided in  Parliament it has already been decided  in Council so we're moving forward to  the try log hoping that this instrument  then will be finalized as soon as  possible  and here is the possibility for all  member states to have common European  funding to invest in their companies in  their smes to help them to make the  transition away from fossil fuels into  for example Renewables cheaper sources  of energy and thus prepare for the  future  we have had a very good Council on all  these topics and I think I will stop  here and I'll be happy to take questions  thank you madam president we'll take a  few questions indeed Irene you were  first  please  so I would like to ask you why did it  say take so long to have an agreement  um could you blame some member states  for being more selfish than others  despite the fact that we Face such as a  crisis thank you  no we are we are all extremely serious  and this is a an extremely serious topic  and also a difficult topic a complex  topic it was very important to make sure  that you are all very very clear about  what we are deciding because what we  have decided is the the very strong  framework and it will play a fundamental  role in order to to reach the goal that  we have determined and you know because  we we knew that it would be a difficult  European tour in fact the fact that we  were able to have an agreement only in a  few hours in is at the contrary in my  opinion a very strong signal of a United  approach and determination to work  together in a European way in fact the  surprise is the fact that we are able in  a very short period of time in a few  hours to get an agreement on such a  difficult topic  I also  um have witnessed that we had intensive  but very constructive discussions and  there was this strong will you could  feel it in the European Council to come  to a common conclusion and of course  different member states have different  priorities but if you look at the steps  we've made forward now this road map  that now has to be worked on and then  implemented it is a joint purchase big  step forward it is the rules for sharing  gas so the solidarity agreements and the  rules that have to be followed in case  of a severe disruption it is the topic  of excessive price prices and how to  limit them and there are two different  models are on the table now to be worked  on the one is on the ttf level  so the overall gas  gas trading level the ttf and the other  is looking at gas that produces  electricity and that's that determines  the price of electricity and then we had  on top the big topic of investment in  European small and medium Enterprises  and in European industry all over Europe  to prepare them for the future so to  help them to bridge this difficult time  of high energy prices to be able to move  forward and to modernize so a big agenda  and for that I must say it was a  relatively short time  Francesca basso Correa  today results  when will European citizens be able to  see the effect of today agreements  because we waited a lot  thank you  I'm confident that very soon the effects  will be we will be will be seen because  I think that we sent also a clear signal  to the markets it means that we are  ready to act together that we are able  to act together and it's there is a  strong political way that's why I'm  confident that there will be a fairly  soon and of course we need to work very  hard and urgently in order to implement  as much as possible the different  measures that are on the table  so um  European citizens will over time  seeing the effects of our efforts  ongoing  let me allow to have a Look Backwards  with you  at the beginning of this horrible War  if we look at the eight months that have  passed since then  Russia has cut two-thirds of all its gas  supplies to Europe two-thirds that's  more than 100 billi