rk together and to do that by building  for example a Consortium which is a big  economic Advantage for the companies  because you increase massively your  Market power and there is a smaller  amount that is binding in the demand  aggregation what does that mean it means  for 15  of the storage companies should tender  or put forward publicly their demand  together that's the binding element then  offers will come and of course every  company is free to choose whether they  take the offer or not so that is the way  the joint procurement is organized but  it's of course a big incentive if you  are able to to build con a Consortium  and on your third part  um households and businesses  indeed there are several  options for member states that we  offer to support because we all know  that there is different fiscal space in  the member states and if we want to have  a Level Playing Field if we want to have  the same opportunity in our single  Market we have to offer to all member  states options to support their  households but also to support their  companies there is first of all the  so-called windfall profits so the  excessive profits of energy producing  companies can be skimmed and invested to  support  households many member states are doing  that are choosing that we have enabled  that a few weeks ago the second point is  that 40 billion of unspent funds from  the last mff  are still available we flexibilize them  so member states can take this money and  invest it into supporting households and  businesses  and the third element is the work on  repower EU  as I said I hope before the end of the  year it will be agreed between Council  and Parliament and repower EU is  investment in infrastructure  cross-border projects Renewables Energy  Efficiency and can be up to 300 billion  euros it depends a bit on what the  choice of member states is but here you  see  besides the state aid three different  options for the different situation  member states have to invest not only in  households but also in companies  thank you madam president Mr President  tomorrow we convene again at 10 A.M and  we'll have another press conference in  the afternoon please have a good night

